            "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo></math> let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></math> be the number of subsets of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>, each containing five elements out of which exactly <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> are odd. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo></math>",
